🏎️ F1 Race Time Prediction Using Qualifying Performance

This project predicts Formula 1 race performance by leveraging AI and machine learning on qualifying data. By combining FastF1 race telemetry with predictive modeling, it forecasts which drivers are most likely to dominate an upcoming Grand Prix.

📂 Project Overview
Objective: Predict race pace and finishing performance from qualifying results.
Target GP: 2025 Chinese Grand Prix

Data Sources:
FastF1 API — Real 2024 Chinese GP lap times and telemetry.
Manually defined 2025 qualifying times — simulated input.
Model Used: Gradient Boosting Regressor (from scikit-learn) with polynomial feature engineering.
AI Role: Model optimization, feature selection, and predictions fine-tuned using AI-driven insights.

⚙️ Technologies & Libraries
fastf1 → Accessing official F1 lap time & telemetry data
pandas, numpy → Data preprocessing and analysis
scikit-learn → Machine learning model building & evaluation
Python 3.10+
(Optional Future) → matplotlib, plotly for race visualization

📊 Methodology
1️⃣ Data Collection
Pulled 2024 Chinese GP race lap data using FastF1.
Created 2025 Qualifying dataset (assumed values for drivers).

2️⃣ Data Mapping
Mapped each driver with:
Code (e.g., VER → Max Verstappen)
Team (e.g., Ferrari, Red Bull, McLaren)
Country
Logo/Emoji for visualization flair

3️⃣ Model Training
X (Features) → Weighted qualifying times + laps completed
y (Target) → Actual lap times from race data
Applied Gradient Boosting Regressor (robust for small, nonlinear datasets).
Evaluated with Mean Absolute Error (MAE) to check accuracy.

4️⃣ Prediction
Predicted lap times for 2025 drivers.
Estimated total race time assuming 51 laps (Shanghai GP).
Ranked drivers by predicted total race performance.

📌 Example Output
🏁 Predicted Top 5 Finishers — 2025 Chinese GP 🏁

🥇 Max Verstappen (Red Bull 🇳🇱) — Predicted Race Time: 90.728 s
🥈 Oscar Piastri (McLaren 🇦🇺) — 90.754 s
🥉 Lando Norris (McLaren 🇬🇧) — 90.781 s
🎖️ George Russell (Mercedes 🇬🇧) — 90.822 s
🎖️ Charles Leclerc (Ferrari 🇲🇨) — 90.899 s

🔍 Model Accuracy (MAE): ~0.35 seconds

🧠 Key Insights
Qualifying pace strongly correlates with race performance.
Drivers from historically dominant teams (Red Bull, Mercedes, Ferrari) consistently rank higher.
AI-driven predictions are highly accurate for short-term outcomes, but integrating weather/strategy data will further improve robustness.

🚀 How to Run
Install Dependencies:
pip install fastf1 pandas scikit-learn

Run the Script:
python chinese_gp_25.py
⚠️ Ensure internet access — FastF1 fetches live/historical data.

📁 File Structure
📦 F1-Race-Prediction
 ┣ 📜 chinese_gp_25.py   # Main script
 ┣ 📂 f1_cache/          # FastF1 local cache
 ┗ 📜 README.md

